        "question_title": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\), points \\(D\\) and \\(E\\) are the midpoints of \\(AB\\) and \\(AC\\), respectively. If \\(|BC|=18\\text{ cm}\\), find \\(|DE|\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "By the midpoint theorem, the segment joining the midpoints of two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side and has half its length. Thus \\(|DE|=\\frac{1}{2}|BC|=\\frac{1}{2}\\times18=9\\text{ cm}\\).",
